    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d825-a1">

                <pb facs="0798" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg700"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bonilla to Mr. Everett</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Honduras, Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1900-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November
                                3, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A short time ago I received the dispatch of
                    your excellency under date of October 11 last, in which you stated that the
                    Government of the United States of America <pb facs="0799" n="701"
                        xml:id="pg701"/> recedes from its claim for the punishment of the sentry,
                    Cruz Rosales, but insists on the immediate payment of an indemnity of $10,000
                    gold for the heirs of Mr. Frank S. Pears, which sum must be paid to the order of
                    that legation.</p>
                <p>In accordance with instructions from the President of the Republic, I have the
                    honor to state to your excellency that the Government of Honduras,
                    notwithstanding that it persists in its opinion already stated as regards the
                    irresponsibility of the state in the violent death of Mr. Pears, the discussion
                    having reached an end, and to prevent the affair interrupting the good relations
                    with the Government of the United States, it has resolved to decree the payment
                    of the indemnity claimed.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith an authorized copy of the decree, which puts an end to the
                    regrettable affair.</p>
                <p>In the same way I inclose a draft to the order of your legation to the value of
                    the sum which is ordered to be paid.</p>
                <p>Expecting that your excellency will acknowledge their proper receipt, I sign
                    myself your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cesar Bonilla.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
